    note: Recommended device names for Linux: /dev/sda1 for root volume. /dev/sd[f-p] for data volumes.
          Newer Linux kernels may rename your devices to /dev/xvdf through /dev/xvdp internally, even when the device name entered here 
          (and shown in the details) is /dev/sdf through /dev/sdp.


